{# Google Analytics 4, for every page on the site. The measurement ID lives in
   _data/site.js so it is stated once; blank it there to switch analytics off.

   Only production builds get the real tag, so `npm start` and Netlify deploy
   previews never send hits.

   Set `gaBeacon` before including this on a page that fires an event and then
   immediately navigates away - beacon transport lets the hit outlive the page:

     {% set gaBeacon = true %}
     {% include "analytics.njk" %}

   The no-op stub in the else branch matters for exactly those pages: they call
   gtag() further down, and an undefined gtag would throw and strand the
   visitor on a page that never redirects. #}
{% if site.isProduction and site.googleAnalyticsId %}
  <!-- Google tag (gtag.js) -->
  <script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id={{ site.googleAnalyticsId }}"></script>
  <script>
    window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
    function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
    gtag('js', new Date());

    gtag('config', '{{ site.googleAnalyticsId }}'{% if gaBeacon %}, { transport_type: 'beacon' }{% endif %});
  </script>
{% else %}
  <script>
    /* Analytics is off in this build. Stub gtag so pages that fire events and
       then redirect still work. */
    window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
    function gtag(){ dataLayer.push(arguments); }
  </script>
{% endif %}
